id: pm-web-413z
title: Same-site sibling origins bypass the cookie-authenticated CSRF guard
description: "The custom CSRF middleware protects every state-changing API route, but isCrossSiteRequest treats Sec-Fetch-Site same-site as automatically trusted. A compromised sibling origin such as another unbrained.dev service can send a cookie-authenticated mutation to pm-web; the browser labels it same-site and the current guard allows it before evaluating the mismatched Origin. CodeQL alerts 163 and 164 do not recognize the custom middleware and require evidence-backed false-positive disposition after the real same-site boundary is repaired."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 0
tags[4]: codeql,csrf,hosted-boundary,security
created_at: "2026-08-30T20:50:06.757Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-30T21:39:58.934Z"
author: codex
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: Cookie-authenticated unsafe requests with Sec-Fetch-Site same-site and a foreign Origin are rejected with 403; same-origin requests remain accepted; bearer or non-browser clients without a session cookie retain their documented compatibility; all state-changing API routers remain behind the CSRF middleware; CodeQL alerts 163 and 164 are dispositioned with exact justification; required package gates pass on the exact pushed head.
definition_of_ready: "Reproduced against the real Express middleware with a pm_token cookie, same-site Fetch Metadata, foreign sibling Origin, and a mutating route."
why_now: "The hosted multi-service origin set shares unbrained.dev, making a sibling-origin compromise a practical CSRF boundary; two high-severity scanner alerts are open on main."
reviewer: security-review
risk: high
confidence: high
reporter: codex
severity: high
environment: pm-web 2026.8.29 at 7e09ca9; Express 5.2.1; cookie-authenticated API
repro_steps: "POST through cookieParser and csrfProtection with Cookie pm_token=session, Host pm-web.unbrained.dev, Origin https://evil.unbrained.dev, and Sec-Fetch-Site same-site; the mutation currently returns 204 instead of 403."
expected_result: Sibling-origin cookie-authenticated mutations are rejected before any route handler runs.
actual_result: "The same-site branch returns false without comparing Origin, so the route executes."
affected_version: 2026.8.29
component: HTTP security boundary
customer_impact: A compromised or attacker-controlled sibling origin can perform authenticated state changes for a visiting pm-web user.
comments[7]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-30T21:00:04.518Z",codex,"TDD reproducer ran before implementation: node --import tsx --test test/rate-limit.test.ts produced 12 passes and 3 failures. The sibling-origin request returned 200 instead of 403, the cross-site unauthenticated login returned 200 instead of 403, and direct classification trusted same-site. After the middleware change the same 15-test real-Express suite passed. Independent read-only review also found pm-web-jpa6: GET /pm/graph can install or activate pm-graph and bypass edit permission; that separate unsafe-method/authorization issue is tracked without broadening this focused patch."
  "2026-08-30T21:14:14.441Z",codex,"Authoritative coverage gate passed 434/434 tests across 29 required TypeScript source files. Exact measured aggregate coverage is 69.64% lines, 81.38% branches, and 64.32% functions; src/csrf.ts itself is 100% lines, 96.15% branches, 100% functions. The repository threshold is only 66/80/60, so this is green for the current package gate but not the ecosystem's requested 100/100/100/100 target."
  "2026-08-30T21:22:11.842Z",codex,"Direct npm run release:check passed on the working head: typecheck, docstrings (85 files / 588 declarations), 434/434 tests with real PostgreSQL routes, npm audit (0 vulnerabilities), pack, fresh npm and Bun acceptance, changelog, release-date verification, and publish-attestation verification. The same release command initially failed only inside the linked-test schema sandbox because its injected PM_PATH escaped into the fresh packed-project pm init; direct acceptance created both fresh trackers successfully. Existing upstream reports GH-682/GH-743 cover linked-test workspace and package-lifecycle sandbox collisions, while GH-841 documents nested init target discovery, so no duplicate pm-cli issue was opened."
  "2026-08-30T21:25:37.247Z",codex,"CI first failed before tests because this item was authored with host pm 2026.8.24 while pm-web and CI exact-pin 2026.8.21; the two versions compute incompatible PM history hashes. Targeted dry-run then pinned history-repair re-anchored only pm-web-413z, and pinned pm health --strict-exit now passes with no gate-failing findings. Upgrading pm-web to 2026.8.27 is separately blocked because that version false-flags intact legacy items pm-web-iocm and pm-web-u9mh; upstream GH-1162 tracks the version-dependent hash/replay regression and Dependabot PR #120 demonstrates it."
  "2026-08-30T21:28:33.178Z",codex,"Greptile review on commit 90b1575 found a valid legacy-queue compatibility defect: pre-upgrade IndexedDB records have no csrfToken and would stop replay at the first 403. TDD added two failures first (missing response bootstrap header; legacy replay sent no token), then implemented a same-origin response token plus service-worker fallback. Focused typecheck/docstrings and 26 tests now pass; the regression proves the legacy record is replayed and cleared exactly once without deleting or rewriting pending data."
  "2026-08-30T21:30:49.897Z",codex,"Post-review full coverage gate passed 435/435 tests across 29 required TypeScript source files. Exact aggregate is 69.64% lines, 81.26% branches, and 64.32% functions; src/csrf.ts is 100% lines, 96.00% branches, and 100% functions. These pass the existing 66/80/60 repository thresholds but remain explicitly below the required ecosystem-wide 100/100/100/100 target."
  "2026-08-30T21:39:58.934Z",codex,"Greptile exact-head review found a second valid queue lifecycle edge: pm_token lasts 30 days but csrf_token is a browser-session cookie, so a queued record can carry a stale token after restart. TDD changed the replay fixture to include stale-session-token and failed because no bootstrap occurred. The repair now obtains the current token on every non-empty flush, never persists new queue tokens, ignores legacy stored tokens, preserves the full queue if bootstrap fails, and passes the focused 26-test/type/docstring gates."
